SUMMARY:Updated: The Biltmore Farm Trail Is Fairly Flat and a 6 Mile Round
  Trip—Join Us!
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\n**Update: The Farm Trail 
 and the Arbor Trace Trail are currently closed (as of March 8). If still c
 losed on May 2\, we will walk the Lagoon Trail instead. The start point in
  the same\, but the distance is shorter.**\n\nIn front of the Antler Hill 
 Barn\, by the Playground\, there is a picnic shelter known as the Antler H
 ill Pavillion. We will meet there at 9:30 a.m.\n\nWe will walk the seldom-
 done Farm Trail along the French Broad River edge of the estate property\,
  mostly out and back. Biltmore says it is a 6-mile (10 KM) round trip.\n\n
 Dress for the weather. Bring a protein snack and water. Walking sticks onl
 y if you want them since the walk will be mostly level. Tennis shoes shoul
 d be okay\, unless it has rained a lot recently\, in which case light hiki
 ng boots would be better. Dogs are welcome. Trail strollers should work ok
 .\n\nYou will need a grounds pass\, so arrive no later than 9 a.m. to purc
 hase it and let me know so we will wait to start the walk until you have j
 oined us. We actually recommend the purchase of an annual pass\, as we wil
 l be walking on the estate grounds several times in the coming year.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/313050558/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260125T170241Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260125T170241Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
