SUMMARY:Gardens of Haywood Community College + 3 Laps of the Bobcat Trail
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nThree laps on the Bobcat 
 Trail amounts to 3.1 miles. Bobcat consists of both natural and paved surf
 aces. There is a little elevation change on the route\, but nothing too st
 renuous.\n\nWe will stop to look at a different garden on each countercloc
 kwise lap. The first lap we will stop at the Bird and Butterfly Garden. Th
 e second lap we will stop at the Dahlia Garden. The third lap we will stop
  at the Rhododendron Garden. All three should be in beautiful bloom. Bring
  your camera!\n\nAs you enter the campus from Jones Cove Road\, go to the 
 first parking lot on the left. We will gather there and then head out.\n\n
 Be sure to dress for the weather. Consider sunscreen and a hat. I'm going 
 to wear tennis shoes\, unless it has rained a lot recently (in which case\
 , I will wear light hiking boots). I plan to bring my walking sticks.\n\nA
 s always\, you are urged to bring plenty of water and a protein snack. Dog
 s are welcome. Trail strollers should not have much problem. There are no 
 bathrooms available that afternoon\, so take care of such needs before you
  arrive.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/314015283/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260329T120118Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260329T120118Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
