SUMMARY:Bonsai Update: Walking the Forest Meadow at the NC Arboretum
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\n**Bonsai Update: The Bons
 ai in the Blue Ridge ticketed event will be going on June 4 – 7. You ver
 y well may want to stay after the walk for lunch and the Bonsai event. Pla
 n accordingly.**\n\nMeet inside the Baker Visitor Center at 09:30 a.m. Res
 trooms are available at the start point.\n\nWe will walk through the Forma
 l Gardens and the Bonsai Exhibit. Then we will make our way to the Forest 
 Meadow\, walking around all the paths. We'll go down Running Cedar Road\, 
 across on Bent Creek Road (taking the Creekside Trails)\, and return on We
 sley Branch Road.\n\nDress for the weather\; consider a hat and sunscreen.
  Some may want walking poles. Sneakers should be fine\, unless it has rain
 ed recently. Be sure to bring plenty of water and a protein snack.\n\nDogs
  on leash are welcome\, but are not allowed in buildings or the Bonsai Exh
 ibit. Trail strollers should be ok.\n\nThe NC Arboretum does not have an a
 dmission fee\, but they charge $20 per car parking fee (so pack as many pe
 ople in your car as you can). We recommend for the driver to purchase the 
 lowest level annual membership which includes free parking. (Of course\, y
 ou may want a higher level membership\, your choice.) We walk at the Arbor
 etum at least six times per year.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/313358020/
